From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:35:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kepler_compute: EDEN_NX2_NO_UPLOAD_STORE=1 stops native channels listing their uploads

Core patch, after 0262. Off unless the switch is set.

Every exec_upload adds a 24-byte entry to uploads, and only the older class's launch method reads and clears
that list. A native channel never gets there: ProcessNativeMethod's default case returns true for everything
but exec_upload and data_upload. So the list only grew, about 2,900 entries a second. Its heap block was 96 MiB
at 13 min and 192 at 24 min, plus 24 on a second channel. The next doubling needs 192 and 384 at once, at about
48 min by the same rate (a guess).

With the switch a native channel stores nothing. The older class is unchanged. Nothing else reads the list, so
picture and speed should not move.

The change is right with or without a switch. The switch only keeps this series' rule, and can go after a run.

Proof in a run: the site at T45's offset 161854d, which moves with each build, gone from EDEN_HEAP_SITE.

Compiled with the build's flags, syntax only. Not linked, not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp b/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
index 9017f9e..34b195e 100644
--- a/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
@@ -38,6 +38,19 @@
 
 namespace Tegra::Engines {
 
+namespace {
+// EDEN_NX2_NO_UPLOAD_STORE=1: a native channel doesn't list its inline uploads. Only the older
+// class's launch method reads that list and clears it, and ProcessNativeMethod never lets a native
+// channel get there, so the list only grew: 24 bytes an upload, about 2,900 a second.
+bool NoUploadStore() {
+    static const bool no_store = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_NO_UPLOAD_STORE");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+    }();
+    return no_store;
+}
+} // Anonymous namespace
+
 KeplerCompute::KeplerCompute(MemoryManager& memory_manager_)
     : memory_manager{memory_manager_}
     , upload_state{memory_manager, regs.upload}
@@ -470,7 +483,9 @@ void KeplerCompute::CallMethod(Core::System& system, u32 method, u32 method_argu
                         .exec_address = upload_state.ExecTargetAddress(),
                         .copy_size = upload_state.GetUploadSize(),
                         .was_dirty = upload_dirty};
-        uploads.push_back(info);
+        if (!native_mode || !NoUploadStore()) {
+            uploads.push_back(info);
+        }
         upload_state.ProcessExec(regs.exec_upload.linear != 0);
         break;
     }
